---
description: >
  GENERAL DEVELOPMENT RULES - Navi Whisper Lux
  
  Documentation:
  - NEVER create .md files unless explicitly requested - This means NO .md files, period
  - No TEMPORAL_INTEGRATION.md, QUICK_TEST.md, SUMMARY.md, or any other .md files
  - Code should be self-documenting - Write clear code, not docs about the code
  - Update ONLY .cursor/rules/*.mdc files - If you need to document something, update rule files
  - No completion reports, summaries, guides, or how-to docs - I'll ask if I want to know something
  - Focus on shipping code - Not documentation about code
  
  Code Quality:
  - Do not add unnecessary fallbacks to fix issues; fix the implementation for simpler, more elegant solutions
  - This does not apply for retry fallbacks when sensible
  
  API Testing (MANDATORY):
  - When adding ANY new backend API endpoint, you MUST add a corresponding test to /back-end/src/tests/api-test-suite.ts
  - Tests must validate: HTTP status codes, response structure, authentication/authorization, and error handling
  - Add tests to the appropriate group: publicTests, authTests, agentWorkflowTests, or blueprintWorkflowTests
  - Run `npm run test:api` to verify all tests pass
  - Pre-commit hook will automatically run all tests and block commits if any fail

apply:
  when: always
---
